    {
      "id": "kug05af",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10.1 Number System"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Digital computers use the binary number system (base 2) consisting of digits 0 and 1 for internal processing and storage.",
        "Octal (base 8) and Hexadecimal (base 16) systems serve as shorthand representations of binary data.",
        "Hexadecimal uses digits 0-9 and letters A-F to represent decimal values from 0 to 15.",
        "Binary conversions require grouping bits in sets of 3 for Octal and sets of 4 for Hexadecimal.",
        "ASCII stands for American Standard Code for Information Interchange and provides standardized encoding for text and characters."
      ],
      "id": "p25e452"
    },
